            <ArticleTitle>[Adrenergic mechanisms of pain regulation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>26-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors briefly account the opioidergic regulation of pain and postulate a concept of adrenergic pain-relieving systems. They also analyze the analgetic and vegetocorrecting effects of clofelin and its benefits as a centrally acting non-opiate analgetic. They discuss the status and prospects for optimization of non-opiate anesthesia in clinical practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
